1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:28,000
*music*

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,100
I have not met yet. My name is Ryan. I have the privilege of being one of the pastors here.

3
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:45,560
So excited to continue our series, our Frequently Asked Questions, What Does the Bible Say About? series.

4
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:52,600
Two weeks ago we launched this series and I talked about specifically how do we approach the Bible when answering our questions.

5
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:55,380
The Bible is both divine and human.

6
00:00:55,980 --> 00:01:02,680
It is this delicate balance similar to the similar to the person and work of Jesus that he is fully human and fully God.

7
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:09,260
The Bible is fully human and fully divine and so we should read it as a unified story that points us to Jesus.

8
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:17,960
It should be read in the cultural context that it was written and so it's important that we think about how to read the Bible.

9
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:25,760
Last week I thought I was being clever and I decided to give the hardest question that we have that we are going to deal with throughout the series to a guest speaker.

10
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:31,940
I have learned my lesson when giving hard questions to guest speakers.

11
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:38,260
He doesn't know you guys and so I've gotten a lot of questions about what do we believe about politics?

12
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:43,080
Because that guy said we were Amish and pacifist.

13
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:45,640
So I gave him a hard question.

14
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:53,500
I'm going to do my best in like two minutes to give you my Cliff Notes version of what I was hoping that he would say and what I think ultimately he was trying to say.

15
00:01:53,500 --> 00:02:00,040
And again, all of you know who read Cliff Notes, they have no context, right?

16
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,360
There's no nuance.

17
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:04,940
So I'm about to bullet point list my takeaways.

18
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:07,420
Cliff Notes, remember.

19
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:10,940
No nuance, no context.

20
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:15,660
If you want nuance and context, come talk to me, please.

21
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:16,720
All right.

22
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:21,400
Citizenship to the kingdom of God is the Christian's primary citizenship.

23
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:27,260
We first and foremost are citizens of the kingdom of God over and above America.

24
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:31,760
Because of this, unity in the family of God should be our top priority.

25
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:36,700
We will not always agree, but we must learn to live with one another in love.

26
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:49,560
This is something that the American church struggles with, that individual Christians struggle with when people are in the family of God and have wildly different opinions about us on earthly politics.

27
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:54,980
It's difficult to live in unity, but we must pursue unity in the midst of diversity.

28
00:02:55,220 --> 00:03:12,440
And the reality is disagreement is often unavoidable because some democratic positions tend to align with kingdom values, like caring for the poor and marginalized, racial justice, inequality, while other primary kingdom values line up with more Republican positions, like the sanctity of human life.

29
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:28,440
This disagreement, when worked out in a loving and unified community, actually helps us better embody God's kingdom on earth as it is in heaven until he returns and rights all of our wrongs.

30
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:36,080
It's important that even if we have differing opinions, that we do so in love and in unity with one another.

31
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:43,940
Finally, whether you choose to vote all red, all blue, a split ticket, or not at all, do so through thoughtful prayer and research.

32
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:51,860
And realize that your participation in the flourishing of society does not stop at the polls, goes beyond the polls.

33
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:56,480
We should be involved in helping solve the problems of this broken world in tangible ways.

34
00:03:56,480 --> 00:04:02,440
Again, cliff notes, lack of nuance and context around emotionally charged topics.

35
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:05,340
If you struggle with some of those things, I'd love to have a conversation.

36
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:07,160
I've already had multiple conversations this week.

37
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:09,100
Plan to continue having those conversations.

38
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:14,120
Let us first and foremost seek God's kingdom on earth as it is in heaven until he returns.

39
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:14,540
Sound good?

40
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:17,440
All right, let's pray and get started on this week's message.

41
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:25,360
Father, we are so grateful for another opportunity to gather together as the body of believers, the family of God.

42
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:32,380
From every tribe, language, tongue, nation, with multiple different backgrounds and histories,

43
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:40,340
God, you have brought us here together and you've called us to unity through the blood of Jesus Christ.

44
00:04:40,340 --> 00:04:43,340
May we honor you with our time today.

45
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:48,660
May you speak through me and may we hear what you have for us to hear.

46
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:50,680
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

47
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:51,540
Amen.

48
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:55,600
All right, this morning we are going to attempt to cover two questions.

49
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,860
One will take the most of our time.

50
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:59,660
The second we will end with.

51
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:01,260
The two questions are this.

52
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:03,800
What is the gospel?

53
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:06,080
Question number one, what is the gospel?

54
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:10,060
And question number two, how do I know if I am saved?

55
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:12,620
And the person that asked the question, what is the gospel?

56
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:14,940
They provided some context that I thought was really helpful.

57
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:20,080
They said, one of our core values at Canvas Community Church, and some of you might know this, some of you might not.

58
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:23,980
One of our core values is that we unite for the sake of the gospel.

59
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:33,560
And the person asking the question said, I hear us talking a lot about unity, but what if we're not all saying the same thing when we say the gospel?

60
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:34,240
Right?

61
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:39,180
It's important that if we're going to unite for the sake of the gospel, the gospel is a big word that means a lot of things to a lot of people.

62
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:46,040
And so I'd love to hear what the church believes, what you believe when you say the gospel.

63
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:49,120
So we're going to do our best to answer that question.

64
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:58,780
If you're in here and you're like, this seems pretty basic, pretty simple, hopefully I think you'll see that the gospel is much bigger and more beautiful than we tend to understand or realize,

65
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:03,240
especially when we seek to summarize it in a presentation for someone who doesn't know Jesus.

66
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:09,320
And also, if you're in here and you're like, I know for a fact that I'm saved, then I would plead with you this morning

67
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:15,480
to spend time in prayer throughout the service for the person in these chairs that has not yet received that message,

68
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,500
that they would do so by the end of our talk.

69
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:18,280
Does that sound good?

70
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,620
All right.

71
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:21,000
I brought a prop.

72
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:25,720
This, my friends, is my bow target.

73
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:28,600
I use this when sighting in my bow.

74
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:36,100
And what you'll notice about this bow target is there's multiple bullseye, bullseye, how do you say that plural?

75
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:37,620
I should have practiced this.

76
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:41,260
There's multiple bullseyes on the target.

77
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:50,080
And I bring this up because I think the reality is, how I want to illustrate this today is the gospel is the target.

78
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:56,140
The gospel is this massive message about God's kingdom coming to earth as it is in heaven.

79
00:06:56,140 --> 00:07:02,780
And the gospel is what Kent read in 1 Corinthians 15, that Jesus came, died, and he did so according to the Scriptures.

80
00:07:02,780 --> 00:07:05,640
That's a big message.

81
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:10,640
The message of God's redemption from Genesis chapter 1 all the way through Revelation.

82
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:11,760
This is a big message.

83
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,580
The gospel is a big target.

84
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:24,500
But what I think tends to happen is when we do our best to summarize the message of the gospel and to boil it down into a three-minute explanation to try and convince somebody to give their life to Jesus, to convert.

85
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:33,640
When we summarize it down into just enough text to put on a small piece of paper that looks like a $100 bill so that we can trick people into reading about Jesus.

86
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:41,020
What tends to happen is when we summarize the message out of a good heart, right?

87
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:42,100
We want to get clear.

88
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:45,660
We want to clearly distill the message of the gospel in a way that people can understand.

89
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:54,260
And I think what tends to happen is we tend to create targets that aren't actually at the center of what the gospel is all about.

90
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:58,160
And so what I want to do today is I want to define the whole target.

91
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:59,360
What is the gospel?

92
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:01,520
What does Jesus mean when he says the gospel?

93
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,920
What do the Scriptures mean when he talks about the gospel?

94
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:09,780
And then I want to talk about some ways in which maybe we've pulled the bullseye a little bit off center.

95
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,680
It's still the gospel.

96
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,040
It's still right and true.

97
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:19,420
But sometimes we overemphasize things or underemphasize things or leave some things out in our presentation of the gospel.

98
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:24,540
And then hopefully at the end, we figure out exactly what the bullseye is.

99
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:25,360
That sound good?

100
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:27,760
Okay.

101
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:31,820
So let's define gospel, the target.

102
00:08:31,820 --> 00:08:33,360
Who wants to learn a little bit of Greek?

103
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:34,560
I probably won't pronounce it right.

104
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:35,880
And you might not even know this.

105
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:46,120
The circles that I run into, there are different types of nerds of people who get in fights over how a dead language is pronounced.

106
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:49,020
And so some of you are going to hear me pronounce it.

107
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:49,760
You're like, that's not.

108
00:08:49,760 --> 00:08:54,060
If you run in these circles, they literally fight over how to pronounce the dead language.

109
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:54,980
Is that fun or what?

110
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:56,420
No wonder Christians don't get along.

111
00:08:56,420 --> 00:08:56,920
All right.

112
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:01,460
So the word gospel, euangelion.

113
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:02,960
I think we have it on the screen.

114
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,320
Maybe.

115
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:07,260
You probably, I mean, just look for the one that doesn't look like English.

116
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:09,720
Maybe it's not there.

117
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:10,760
It's fine if it's not there.

118
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:13,940
Euangelion is the word for gospel.

119
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:20,760
And nowadays, this word gospel is pretty much just used in Christian or religious settings.

120
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:27,280
How many of you go around talking about the gospel of Fox News?

121
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,860
That's not what we say, right?

122
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:29,620
We don't say that.

123
00:09:29,620 --> 00:09:31,440
We don't use the word that way.

124
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:35,340
It has become pretty much just a religious spiritual word.

125
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:37,420
But this was not the case in the first century.

126
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:44,940
Euangelion, good news, gospel, was a word regularly used by earthly kingdoms in a political way.

127
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:57,980
For instance, when Caesar Augustus established the Roman Empire, he sent out messengers to proclaim the gospel, the euangelion of the Roman Empire, that would lead to peace and salvation to its citizens.

128
00:09:58,080 --> 00:10:05,560
It's a word that in the first century would have been recognized as an announcement that a new king was in power.

129
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,260
A new leader had arrived.

130
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:08,860
A new kingdom had been established.

131
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:15,140
And that kingdom would lead to peace and salvation for its people on earth.

132
00:10:15,140 --> 00:10:24,080
So, when Jesus showed up on the scene, this is exactly what he does in Mark chapter 1.

133
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:33,420
Mark chapter 1, verses 14 and 15, Jesus went to Galilee where he preached God's gospel, euangelion.

134
00:10:33,420 --> 00:10:38,440
Now, I wonder if Jesus' gospel sounds anything like the gospel that we preach on a regular basis.

135
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:42,640
This is Jesus' one-sentence summary of the gospel of Jesus.

136
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:45,800
Let me find it.

137
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:46,740
He went to Galilee.

138
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:47,980
He preached God's gospel.

139
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:51,240
The time promised by God has come at last.

140
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,700
The kingdom of God is near.

141
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:57,420
Repent of your sins and believe the gospel.

142
00:10:57,420 --> 00:11:01,360
Does that sound like what we typically preach when we preach the gospel?

143
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,420
Bits and pieces, right?

144
00:11:03,420 --> 00:11:05,640
Kind of, but not really.

145
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:07,620
What happened there?

146
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:12,380
Why did we start preaching a gospel that's different than the gospel of Jesus?

147
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:17,160
See, the original audience, when they would have heard Jesus proclaiming this,

148
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:21,600
they would have not just heard some purely spiritual message about what happens to you when you die.

149
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:27,640
They would have heard an announcement about a new leader who came to launch a new kingdom.

150
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:31,980
And in their minds, that kingdom would bring about earthly salvation.

151
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:41,380
The good Jews in the room who were listening to this talk, they would have known that this wasn't just an ordinary kingdom.

152
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:44,320
This wasn't some new, unexpected kingdom.

153
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:50,080
This was the one true kingdom that has been promised from the very beginning of Scripture.

154
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:52,920
They would have known what Jesus was doing.

155
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:57,180
From the beginning of the Hebrew Scriptures, God has set up his kingdom.

156
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:59,980
Genesis 1 and 2, Adam and Eve in the garden.

157
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:03,860
This is God's kingdom, his rule and reign over his image bearers.

158
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:08,780
You submit to me and you will have an eternal and blessed life.

159
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:09,760
You reject me.

160
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:12,340
You worship idols.

161
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:15,500
You choose to not follow me.

162
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:20,400
And you will experience the consequences of that decision.

163
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:26,440
So from Genesis chapter 3, humanity has been believing a number of other Gospels.

164
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:30,100
Submitting their lives to a number of other kingdoms.

165
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:35,020
And again, because we don't use this language, we don't use this language about anything else.

166
00:12:35,020 --> 00:12:37,000
It might seem a little bit weird.

167
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,240
But we do.

168
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:43,780
We believe the gospel of money, of power, of sex, of comfort, of religion, of nation.

169
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:45,520
And on and on the list could go.

170
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:49,680
We have chosen to deny God's rightful rule over our lives.

171
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:52,960
And we have bowed down to idols that were created by God.

172
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:59,460
Genesis chapter 3 says this is the bruising of humanity's heel.

173
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:07,180
All of the brokenness of this world is a result of us refusing God's gospel, God's kingdom,

174
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:09,540
his rule and reign over all of creation.

175
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:11,260
And again, we talked about it a couple weeks ago.

176
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:18,240
From Genesis through the end of the Old Testament is story after story after story of God's chosen people,

177
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:21,500
the nation of Israel, the people who were supposed to receive the gospel,

178
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:25,700
believe in the kingdom of God, let God's rule and reign carry over them.

179
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:33,420
They rejected him again and again and again, bowed down to idols, created gods that were made out of human things.

180
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:40,240
But from the beginning of Scripture, God has promised that he would send forth one true human,

181
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:44,840
one representative for the human race who would redeem humanity from their idolatry.

182
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:47,660
It's a hard word to say when you're talking fast.

183
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,560
And show them how to be truly human.

184
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:56,460
Although the enemy, the snake, the serpent, the evil one, although he bruised our heel,

185
00:13:56,460 --> 00:14:00,000
one true human would come and he would crush his head.

186
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Jesus steps in and says the promised time of God has come at last.

187
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:13,700
The one true human is here to establish God's kingdom, his rule, his reign.

188
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:17,200
Once and for all, he is here to crush the head of the serpent,

189
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:22,760
to have victory over the evil and demonic forces that so often take over our world.

190
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:28,780
This person would declare God's kingdom had come.

191
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:31,420
Again, remember I said every good Jew would have picked up on this.

192
00:14:31,420 --> 00:14:37,480
This is what Isaiah, the Jewish prophet, told the Jews to look out for when salvation would come.

193
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,080
It says this,

194
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:52,160
This is the good news.

195
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:57,100
The good news is any time that God has his proper rule and reign over humanity,

196
00:14:57,100 --> 00:15:00,020
this is when the gospel enters the picture.

197
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:06,160
The plot twist, though, is that the kingdom of God was not going to come the way that people expect it.

198
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:11,760
Again, I said, this is not an overly spiritual word in the first century.

199
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:12,800
They heard kingdom.

200
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:14,620
They heard the gospel and they were thinking,

201
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:16,720
Okay, Jesus is about to take power.

202
00:15:16,720 --> 00:15:18,800
He's about to defeat Rome.

203
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,880
He's about to have victory over our enemies.

204
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:23,420
They see him healing blind people.

205
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:28,960
They see him feeding, you know, 5,000 people with a small lunchbox.

206
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:33,860
And they're like, Okay, this guy has the power to overcome the earthly forces in Rome.

207
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:36,360
They had this idea in their head.

208
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:42,420
And it fell woefully short of what God would actually do through Jesus on the cross.

209
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:47,100
See, Jesus didn't just take power over earthly kingdoms.

210
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:57,240
Jesus laid down his life and he defeated the spiritual enemies behind every earthly enemy through his sacrificial love and forgiveness.

211
00:15:57,240 --> 00:16:03,660
The cross of Christ was viewed by Rome and the religious Jews as victory over a lunatic religious leader.

212
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:08,060
But in reality, it is the symbol of God's victory over sin and death.

213
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:09,920
Colossians chapter 2.

214
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:10,440
Listen to this.

215
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:11,160
This is so beautiful.

216
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:12,300
This is the gospel.

217
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:13,860
This is the power of the gospel.

218
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:14,980
2, 13, and 14.

219
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:18,700
Jesus canceled, or God canceled the record of charges against us.

220
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:21,020
He took it away by nailing it to the cross.

221
00:16:21,020 --> 00:16:24,540
In this way, he disarmed the spiritual rulers and authorities.

222
00:16:24,540 --> 00:16:28,300
He shamed them publicly by his victory over them on the cross.

223
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:34,120
What looked to the world like defeat was actually spiritual victory.

224
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:42,180
The one true human would crush the head of the serpent through his sacrificial death, burial, and resurrection.

225
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:50,980
My point here is that when we define the gospel, we should be careful not to shrink it down to be much smaller and less significant than it actually is.

226
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:58,280
The gospel is not, it's not that what we mean when we say the gospel isn't true.

227
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:02,040
It's just that what we mean is usually a much smaller piece of the entire pie.

228
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:04,600
The gospel is the target.

229
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:09,320
It is much bigger and more beautiful and more far-reaching than we typically acknowledge.

230
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:11,360
I love what Scott McKnight says.

231
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:14,740
He says, the Gospels are the gospel.

232
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:24,480
Anytime we talk about Christ's arrival, Christ's life, Christ's teachings, Christ's death, Christ's resurrection, this is all the gospel.

233
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:28,040
Everything about what Jesus did, what he came to do, it is.

234
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:29,020
The gospel.

235
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:35,260
Anytime we talk about the good news that God's kingdom has come to earth through Jesus, we are gospeling.

236
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:44,580
I would summarize it this way, and I think, I don't know, those of you that have been coming for a while might realize that I would call myself the king of run-on sentences.

237
00:17:45,580 --> 00:17:46,820
So, prepare yourself.

238
00:17:46,820 --> 00:17:49,480
I have contributed yet again to my masterpiece.

239
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:52,980
This is how I'd summarize the gospel.

240
00:17:52,980 --> 00:18:01,060
The gospel is the good news that God reconciles individuals to himself through Jesus' life, death, resurrection, and ascension,

241
00:18:01,640 --> 00:18:11,180
forming a new multi-ethnic family of God who demonstrates together the values of the kingdom of God on earth as it is in heaven until he returns.

242
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:17,380
The promised time has come.

243
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:19,820
God's kingdom is at hand.

244
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:23,160
Repent and believe.

245
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:28,860
The inauguration of God's kingdom through Christ's life, death, and resurrection, it has implications.

246
00:18:28,860 --> 00:18:30,840
And this is where I think we get a little bit off track.

247
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:40,960
It has implications for individuals both on earth and in eternity, and it has implications for institutions, for groups of people on earth and in eternity.

248
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,520
So, let me throw up the chart.

249
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:45,240
This chart will represent my bow target, right?

250
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:46,600
Whole target.

251
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:47,540
The gospel.

252
00:18:47,540 --> 00:18:48,620
The good news of Jesus.

253
00:18:48,620 --> 00:18:49,960
The kingdom has come.

254
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,080
The time is at hand.

255
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:56,000
The God of Israel rules and reigns because of what Jesus did.

256
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,320
Is that good news or what?

257
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,020
All right.

258
00:19:00,020 --> 00:19:09,620
Now, I think when we try and summarize the gospel, when we try and boil it down to a three-minute speech so we can give to somebody on the elevator to tell them how to become a Christian,

259
00:19:10,220 --> 00:19:15,120
I think what happens is we tend to get pulled away from the center of the target.

260
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:21,940
And, again, I'm not saying that what I'm about to say about all four of these targets, I'm not saying they're not the gospel.

261
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:27,000
I'm saying they're an emphasis on the gospel that might pull us a little bit away from the center bullseye.

262
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,140
I'm going to pick on everybody, right?

263
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:32,760
Equal opportunity offender.

264
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:33,940
I've used this term before.

265
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:37,680
So, if you're offended by one or you're not offended by one, don't worry.

266
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:38,860
Your time is coming, okay?

267
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:41,120
So, the chart, right?

268
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:47,160
The gospel has implications for individuals both on earth and for eternity.

269
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:52,460
And institutions, probably not the best word, but I'm a pastor and I wanted them to both start with an I.

270
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:55,380
Community, like groups of people, right?

271
00:19:55,380 --> 00:20:01,420
The gospel has institutional implications both on earth and in eternity.

272
00:20:02,220 --> 00:20:03,940
So, which one am I picking on first?

273
00:20:03,940 --> 00:20:08,740
Okay, perfect.

274
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:16,600
The gospel has implications for the individual on earth.

275
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:20,740
I call this the coffee mug gospel, okay?

276
00:20:20,740 --> 00:20:25,640
How many of you guys have coffee mugs with Bible verses on them?

277
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:28,160
Most, many of us, right?

278
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:29,660
Okay.

279
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:37,440
What typically tends to happen with those Bible verses is they are very positive messages about your life on earth.

280
00:20:37,440 --> 00:20:40,400
And they are ripped from their broader context.

281
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:45,460
And it doesn't mean that they're not true or that the implications aren't there.

282
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:52,860
But we tend to make this version of the gospel tends to be that Jesus died so that your life on earth can be blessed.

283
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:55,620
Is that false?

284
00:20:55,620 --> 00:20:56,320
No.

285
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:57,500
But can it be misleading?

286
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:58,240
Absolutely.

287
00:20:58,240 --> 00:21:06,060
This explanation of the gospel emphasizes how the inauguration of God's kingdom through Christ's death and resurrection impacts your individual life on earth.

288
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:08,860
It oversimplifies life in a broken world.

289
00:21:08,860 --> 00:21:15,220
It says that if you just have enough faith in Jesus, your life will be blessed because God has a plan for you.

290
00:21:15,220 --> 00:21:22,800
You can do all things through Christ who strengthens you and everything works together for the good of those who love him and are called according to his purposes.

291
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:24,160
Right?

292
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:26,580
Here's the tension.

293
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:31,440
God very much does emphasize earthly blessings for those who follow him.

294
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:37,220
John chapter 10 verse 10 says, I came to give you life and life more abundantly.

295
00:21:37,220 --> 00:21:43,440
Philippians chapter 4 verse 7 says, the follower of Jesus has peace that passes all understanding.

296
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:47,120
Psalm chapter 23.

297
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:49,720
I mean, just read Psalm chapter 23.

298
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:52,040
He leads us beside still waters.

299
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:55,340
He lets us take a nap in green pastures.

300
00:21:55,340 --> 00:22:01,380
He sets a table in the presence of our enemies like he is blessing us.

301
00:22:01,380 --> 00:22:08,640
And then one of my favorite things, I pray this over my son every night, the prayer that God gave the priest to pray over his people, the nation of Israel.

302
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:11,280
He said, may the Lord bless you and keep you.

303
00:22:11,280 --> 00:22:14,300
May the Lord make his face shine upon you and be gracious to you.

304
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:18,160
May the Lord give you his shalom, his peace.

305
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:20,320
Earthly blessing.

306
00:22:22,260 --> 00:22:27,820
Following Jesus, submitting your life to the kingdom of God, it will bless your individual life on earth.

307
00:22:27,820 --> 00:22:31,060
But maybe not like we think.

308
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:38,560
And when we make this the primary presentation of the gospel, we set people up for failure and disappointment.

309
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:43,780
We invite people to put their hope in a message that is a bit misleading and unrealistic.

310
00:22:44,720 --> 00:23:01,400
What happens when this is the gospel that we preach and the person that received it in hope gets a cancer diagnosis or struggles with infertility for years or faces a financial crisis or goes through a natural disaster or has a miscarriage or is affected by broken relationships.

311
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:15,060
Life with Jesus, I love this, John Mark Homer says this, life with Jesus isn't all up and to the right.

312
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:27,500
But when we overemphasize the gospel in this way, we give people the implication, we give people the thought in their mind that if they just submit enough, if they just have enough faith, their life will be up and to the right.

313
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:28,380
Everything will be better.

314
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:32,300
Life with Jesus isn't all up and to the right.

315
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:38,420
It is a blessed life, but the blessings come from God's presence being with us in the midst of the tragedies of this broken world.

316
00:23:38,420 --> 00:23:49,740
The kingdom of God brings earthly blessings to the individual, but it is not necessarily what we think or how we communicate.

317
00:23:49,740 --> 00:23:50,160
All right.

318
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:51,600
Second one.

319
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:56,420
The gospel is all about the individual life in eternity.

320
00:23:56,420 --> 00:23:59,540
Now is where some people are going to get up and leave.

321
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:02,000
I'm kidding.

322
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:02,520
I'm kidding.

323
00:24:02,520 --> 00:24:03,380
Maybe.

324
00:24:03,380 --> 00:24:03,920
I don't know.

325
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:04,400
We'll find out.

326
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:04,640
All right.

327
00:24:04,640 --> 00:24:10,300
This explanation of the gospel I call the evangelical gospel.

328
00:24:10,300 --> 00:24:17,640
And everyone in the room said, wait, the evangelical gospel is the gospel.

329
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:19,160
You can't be making this a character.

330
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:22,880
It's how we identify ourselves, right?

331
00:24:23,980 --> 00:24:24,300
Okay.

332
00:24:24,300 --> 00:24:26,200
Evangelical gospel.

333
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:34,460
This explanation of the gospel emphasizes how the inauguration of God's kingdom through Christ's death and resurrection impacts your individual life in eternity.

334
00:24:35,740 --> 00:24:41,680
And I think probably this is the emphasis that I think most of us in the room are most familiar with.

335
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:51,160
Focuses on your individual sins before a holy God and your need for Christ's death to cleanse you from your sins so that you can spend eternity with God in heaven.

336
00:24:55,020 --> 00:24:56,440
Is anything I said not true?

337
00:24:56,440 --> 00:24:58,560
No, it's true.

338
00:24:58,560 --> 00:25:01,960
But what happens when we overemphasize it?

339
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:04,040
See, John 3, 16.

340
00:25:04,140 --> 00:25:10,320
For God so loved the world that he gave his only begotten son that whosoever believes in him shall not perish but have everlasting life.

341
00:25:10,320 --> 00:25:15,900
That is a message to an individual to receive eternal life through the gospel of Jesus.

342
00:25:15,900 --> 00:25:17,560
Romans 6, verse 23.

343
00:25:17,560 --> 00:25:22,460
The wages of sin is death, but the gift of God is eternal life.

344
00:25:22,460 --> 00:25:25,000
Jude, verse 21.

345
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:29,820
Await the mercy of Jesus who will bring you eternal life.

346
00:25:30,420 --> 00:25:33,980
The gospel does offer eternal salvation to the individual.

347
00:25:33,980 --> 00:25:41,780
But when we make this the primary focus of the gospel we share, it tends to be all about a one-time decision you make.

348
00:25:41,780 --> 00:25:49,100
A magic prayer that you pray that gets you into heaven when you die, but doesn't require any participation in the kingdom of God on earth.

349
00:25:49,100 --> 00:25:55,220
We try and scare people into heaven.

350
00:25:57,460 --> 00:26:05,240
We're shrinking down the message of Jesus, and we're not inviting them to participate in God's kingdom on earth as it is in heaven.

351
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:08,400
It's true.

352
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:14,100
It's just, if we overemphasize it this way, it can lead us a bit astray.

353
00:26:14,100 --> 00:26:23,060
This emphasis on the gospel also, it has the tendency to make God sound like an angry judge in the sky who wants to kill you for your sins.

354
00:26:23,780 --> 00:26:26,860
But he was feeling nice one day and decided to kill Jesus instead.

355
00:26:26,860 --> 00:26:34,400
Maybe this is my baggage from vacation Bible school growing up.

356
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:43,260
But, like, this gospel, it tends to make God seem really angry and us, like, awful and unacceptable before a holy God.

357
00:26:43,260 --> 00:26:45,700
I'm not saying that there isn't implications for that.

358
00:26:47,460 --> 00:26:49,100
God isn't an angry judge, though.

359
00:26:49,100 --> 00:26:50,460
He's a loving father.

360
00:26:50,460 --> 00:26:58,300
He doesn't just want to secure your eternal destiny, but he wants to transform you from the inside out so that you can be a blessing to those around you.

361
00:26:58,300 --> 00:27:04,420
This focus, it becomes sin and holiness rather than image bearers and a loving father.

362
00:27:06,140 --> 00:27:13,800
We do sin, we do fall short, but we were also created in the image of God, and he has a plan to redeem us and to restore us if we would just trust him.

363
00:27:13,800 --> 00:27:15,840
All right.

364
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:17,640
Next.

365
00:27:17,640 --> 00:27:22,300
The gospel has earthly implications for groups of people.

366
00:27:22,300 --> 00:27:24,500
Yes?

367
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:28,860
I'm worried that this isn't going to work all the way through.

368
00:27:28,860 --> 00:27:29,520
We'll see how it goes.

369
00:27:29,520 --> 00:27:31,940
I call this the social gospel.

370
00:27:31,940 --> 00:27:39,760
It is the explanation of the gospel that emphasizes how God's kingdom through Christ's death and resurrection impacts institutions on earth.

371
00:27:39,760 --> 00:27:47,440
It focuses on the church's command to love and serve the marginalized and oppressed by meeting their earthly needs.

372
00:27:48,900 --> 00:27:54,600
The gospel does very much so have implications on the church taking care of the poor, the widow, and the orphan.

373
00:27:54,600 --> 00:27:58,800
This is an accurate implication of the gospel.

374
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:04,420
Jesus says in Matthew chapter 25, whatever you did for the least of these, you did for me.

375
00:28:04,420 --> 00:28:07,020
What about the parable of the good Samaritan?

376
00:28:07,020 --> 00:28:10,320
All about taking care of those who are in need.

377
00:28:10,320 --> 00:28:16,260
James chapter 2 says, what good is it if you say you have faith but don't show it with your actions?

378
00:28:17,040 --> 00:28:23,260
If you say you believe the gospel but you don't do anything for anyone who is in need, what good is that faith?

379
00:28:23,260 --> 00:28:34,700
The problem is this emphasis can often lead people to think that obedience only includes meeting physical needs apart from sharing the spiritual truth of the gospel.

380
00:28:34,700 --> 00:28:41,840
This approach, there's actually two versions of this approach.

381
00:28:42,880 --> 00:28:47,080
And I would say that it's probably this situation here.

382
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:55,740
Both versions of this approach are probably where most of our political earthly tensions live.

383
00:28:55,740 --> 00:28:56,980
Okay?

384
00:28:56,980 --> 00:29:05,540
The two versions of this approach are one, the more liberal approach, which just says the only responsibility of the Christian

385
00:29:05,540 --> 00:29:08,700
is to meet the needs of those who are in need.

386
00:29:08,700 --> 00:29:17,160
And it totally avoids talking about spiritual idolatry, spiritual truth, separation from a holy God.

387
00:29:17,160 --> 00:29:22,400
It's just, we're just gonna take care of physical needs and we're not gonna talk about Jesus.

388
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:29,340
And hopefully God will somehow incept into their brain that we did it because of Jesus.

389
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:34,340
And then maybe they might receive the gospel and believe in Jesus.

390
00:29:34,340 --> 00:29:35,360
Okay?

391
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:38,600
It emphasizes all grace and no truth.

392
00:29:39,900 --> 00:29:47,160
And we know, those of us who read the Scriptures enough, we know that the Scriptures are littered with a tension between grace and truth.

393
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:49,680
It's Jesus to the woman caught in idolatry.

394
00:29:49,680 --> 00:29:52,320
He stoops down with her on the ground.

395
00:29:52,320 --> 00:29:54,460
He extends grace and compassion to her.

396
00:29:54,460 --> 00:29:57,680
He shames all those who are thinking about stoning her to death.

397
00:29:57,680 --> 00:30:01,320
And then he looks her in the eye and he says, go and sin no more.

398
00:30:01,320 --> 00:30:03,780
There's grace and truth.

399
00:30:03,780 --> 00:30:10,600
And so the social version, the more kind of liberal version of this is we're just gonna take care of people's needs and let God figure out the rest.

400
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:19,440
The other version, the more conservative version of this, is Christians saying we're going to make people obey God through legislation.

401
00:30:19,440 --> 00:30:20,620
Right?

402
00:30:20,620 --> 00:30:29,380
We are going to vote for people in such a way that they are going to make laws that all kind of fall under the umbrella of God's kingdom.

403
00:30:29,380 --> 00:30:36,640
And therefore, people will end up experiencing God's kingdom because they have to, because the law says so.

404
00:30:36,640 --> 00:30:41,340
The problem with that is there's no truth, right?

405
00:30:41,340 --> 00:30:46,040
There's no, it's not inviting people into a transformation of their life from the inside out.

406
00:30:46,040 --> 00:30:48,480
It's just saying, well, we're in charge, so you have to obey.

407
00:30:53,480 --> 00:31:03,020
All four of the Gospels end with a very clear command from Jesus to go and preach the gospel, making disciples of all nations.

408
00:31:03,020 --> 00:31:10,320
We have to balance meeting both physical needs and addressing spiritual needs with grace and truth.

409
00:31:10,320 --> 00:31:12,460
It's not wrong.

410
00:31:12,460 --> 00:31:14,300
It's just an overemphasis.

411
00:31:14,300 --> 00:31:15,440
All right.

412
00:31:15,440 --> 00:31:16,380
Last one.

413
00:31:16,380 --> 00:31:18,080
Let's see here.

414
00:31:22,580 --> 00:31:24,720
I call this the set apart gospel.

415
00:31:24,720 --> 00:31:35,780
This explanation of the gospel emphasizes how the inauguration of God's kingdom through Christ's death and resurrection impacts institutions for eternity.

416
00:31:35,780 --> 00:31:41,760
It focuses on the church's need to live set apart lives as gospel witnesses to the watching world.

417
00:31:41,760 --> 00:31:46,800
It says, oh, the church is called to be together as a called out community.

418
00:31:47,180 --> 00:31:58,360
We are supposed to live in obedience to the gospel of Jesus, the kingdom of God, and all of the people who have not received the gospel outside, they should look at our lives and they should see something different.

419
00:31:58,360 --> 00:32:00,540
They should want what we have.

420
00:32:00,540 --> 00:32:01,580
Does that make sense?

421
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:03,600
Okay.

422
00:32:03,600 --> 00:32:05,480
No, it doesn't, but I got to keep going.

423
00:32:05,480 --> 00:32:06,320
So I'm sorry.

424
00:32:06,320 --> 00:32:09,500
Here's the thing.

425
00:32:09,500 --> 00:32:16,640
God does seem to invite the church to live set apart lives pursuing radical unity with one another in a world filled with idolatry and rebellion.

426
00:32:16,640 --> 00:32:19,080
I think about the Sermon on the Mount.

427
00:32:19,280 --> 00:32:23,320
The church is called to be the salt of the earth, light of the world, a city on a hill.

428
00:32:23,320 --> 00:32:31,060
John 17, Jesus' last prayer for his disciples before he would go to the cross.

429
00:32:31,060 --> 00:32:44,160
This is how the world will know you are my disciples, by your radical unity with one another, by being a family of God in the midst of a world full of sin and idolatry.

430
00:32:45,400 --> 00:32:51,320
1 Timothy 3, the church of the living God, is the pillar and foundation of truth.

431
00:32:51,320 --> 00:32:54,920
This is a good and right implication of the gospel.

432
00:32:54,920 --> 00:33:04,900
The problem is when we overemphasize it, it can cause Christians to overly withdraw from the world around them, losing meaningful opportunities to engage with hurting and lost people.

433
00:33:04,900 --> 00:33:09,180
One of my buddies grew up in a church like this.

434
00:33:10,300 --> 00:33:16,500
When you sing songs, you do not have instruments, because that looks worldly, right?

435
00:33:16,500 --> 00:33:20,860
Man, it's tense in here this morning.

436
00:33:20,860 --> 00:33:22,540
Right?

437
00:33:22,540 --> 00:33:23,120
It's like this.

438
00:33:23,120 --> 00:33:37,480
We have to, by the way we dress, by the way we act, we have to be so other than the world around us that it be obvious to them that we are different, that we serve a different king, we follow a different kingdom.

439
00:33:38,720 --> 00:33:50,640
The problem is we lose out on relationships because the rest of the world doesn't want to have a conversation with a person who doesn't look anything like them or have any understanding of their culture whatsoever.

440
00:33:50,640 --> 00:33:52,780
We're called to be missionaries.

441
00:33:52,780 --> 00:33:56,460
We have to understand the culture around us.

442
00:33:57,420 --> 00:34:10,140
Okay, so all of that, let's try and get to a more centralized understanding of what the gospel is.

443
00:34:10,140 --> 00:34:12,580
What is the bullseye on the target?

444
00:34:12,580 --> 00:34:21,060
I put the cross there at the center because the cross becomes the symbol for what all of the implications of the gospel are, and all of the implications of the gospel are there.

445
00:34:21,280 --> 00:34:23,360
There is an individual and earthly implication.

446
00:34:23,360 --> 00:34:25,780
There is an individual and eternal implication.

447
00:34:25,780 --> 00:34:28,340
There is a group and earthly, a group and eternal.

448
00:34:28,340 --> 00:34:33,160
All of these things find their meaning in the cross of Jesus Christ.

449
00:34:34,160 --> 00:34:39,720
My goal with this message is that we would broaden our understanding of how beautiful and robust the gospel of Jesus is.

450
00:34:39,720 --> 00:34:44,880
The gospel of Jesus is so much more than just how God went about forgiving individual sins.

451
00:34:45,600 --> 00:34:48,020
It's more than just blessing your earthly lives.

452
00:34:48,020 --> 00:34:50,520
It's more than just blessing the world around you.

453
00:34:50,520 --> 00:34:59,580
The gospel is the God of the universe taking on human flesh, confronting the principalities and powers of this fallen world through his sacrificial death,

454
00:34:59,580 --> 00:35:12,760
and inaugurating a new kingdom where people from every tribe, language, and tongue are invited to join a new family who embody God's values on earth as it is in heaven until he returns.

455
00:35:15,600 --> 00:35:21,920
We see this in all of this, in the Lord's Prayer, okay?

456
00:35:21,920 --> 00:35:29,620
The Lord's Prayer is at the center of Christ's most important, most impactful sermon, the Sermon on the Mount.

457
00:35:29,620 --> 00:35:31,600
So it's the center of the center of his teaching.

458
00:35:31,600 --> 00:35:33,060
We've talked about this before.

459
00:35:33,060 --> 00:35:35,960
Listen to this, the Lord's Prayer.

460
00:35:35,960 --> 00:35:39,940
Our Father in heaven, holy is your name.

461
00:35:41,180 --> 00:35:50,500
So this is a prayer that he gives to individuals to pray, and when he instructs individuals to pray, he asks them to pray, our Father, right?

462
00:35:50,500 --> 00:35:53,160
It's both individual and institutional.

463
00:35:53,160 --> 00:35:58,100
It's both for you as a person and for you in the group of people called the church.

464
00:35:58,100 --> 00:36:00,620
Our Father in heaven, holy is your name.

465
00:36:00,620 --> 00:36:02,300
Your kingdom come.

466
00:36:02,300 --> 00:36:05,340
Your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

467
00:36:05,340 --> 00:36:07,500
This is social implications.

468
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:09,620
This is institutional earthly implications.

469
00:36:09,620 --> 00:36:12,380
May your kingdom be visible on earth as it is in heaven.

470
00:36:12,380 --> 00:36:14,440
You want to know what the kingdom of God looks like?

471
00:36:14,440 --> 00:36:15,440
There's no poor people.

472
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:17,080
There's no marginalized people.

473
00:36:17,080 --> 00:36:18,120
There's no war.

474
00:36:18,120 --> 00:36:19,460
There's no chaos.

475
00:36:19,460 --> 00:36:26,900
We're invited to pray and participate in God's kingdom coming to earth now.

476
00:36:26,900 --> 00:36:30,400
Give us this day our daily bread.

477
00:36:30,400 --> 00:36:31,700
Coffee cup, gospel, anybody?

478
00:36:31,700 --> 00:36:32,400
Right?

479
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:34,360
I have physical needs right now.

480
00:36:34,360 --> 00:36:35,380
I have bills to be paid.

481
00:36:35,380 --> 00:36:36,320
I have food to eat.

482
00:36:36,320 --> 00:36:38,740
I need your provision for me now.

483
00:36:38,740 --> 00:36:43,440
Forgive us of our sins as we forgive those who sin against us.

484
00:36:43,440 --> 00:36:46,540
The evangelical gospel is baked into that line.

485
00:36:46,540 --> 00:36:49,640
We need forgiveness from God through Jesus.

486
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:53,580
And that's the only way that we'll be able to extend forgiveness to others.

487
00:36:53,580 --> 00:36:58,860
Lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil one.

488
00:36:58,860 --> 00:37:00,360
Set apart.

489
00:37:00,740 --> 00:37:03,480
May we live lives that are different than the rest of the world.

490
00:37:03,480 --> 00:37:06,120
May we care about the consequences of our sin.

491
00:37:06,120 --> 00:37:09,340
And may we put sin to death for the glory of God and the good of our neighbor.

492
00:37:09,340 --> 00:37:16,860
I long for us to be a church that preaches the gospel that hits the bullseye of this target.

493
00:37:16,860 --> 00:37:21,700
May we be a people who live into the abundant life of Jesus now.

494
00:37:22,120 --> 00:37:27,560
May we grasp the breadth and depth of God's love for us through his gift of eternal salvation.

495
00:37:27,560 --> 00:37:31,800
May we express that love in tangible ways to those around us.

496
00:37:31,800 --> 00:37:42,580
And may we live in a radical, united community with one another who embody the values of the kingdom of God as a gospel witness to the world around us.

497
00:37:42,580 --> 00:37:45,400
This is the good news.

498
00:37:46,520 --> 00:37:50,020
The time promised by God has come at last.

499
00:37:50,020 --> 00:37:55,340
The salvation that God promised from the moment that humanity rebelled in Genesis chapter 3.

500
00:37:55,340 --> 00:38:00,040
The moment the rebellion happens, God promises a restoration, a salvation.

501
00:38:00,040 --> 00:38:00,620
It's coming.

502
00:38:00,620 --> 00:38:03,300
Throughout the prophets, he's prophesying the time is coming.

503
00:38:03,300 --> 00:38:04,020
The time is coming.

504
00:38:04,020 --> 00:38:04,720
The time is coming.

505
00:38:04,720 --> 00:38:08,520
One human, one representative of the nation of Israel will come.

506
00:38:08,520 --> 00:38:14,540
And he will finally, once and for all, have victory over sin and the demonic forces and the powers.

507
00:38:14,860 --> 00:38:16,360
And he will establish his kingdom.

508
00:38:16,360 --> 00:38:20,460
And Jesus shows up and he said, the promised time of God has come.

509
00:38:20,460 --> 00:38:21,720
The kingdom of God is here.

510
00:38:21,720 --> 00:38:23,120
Repent.

511
00:38:23,120 --> 00:38:24,280
Believe.

512
00:38:24,280 --> 00:38:28,400
So, that leads us to, how do I know if I'm saved?

513
00:38:28,400 --> 00:38:28,940
I promise.

514
00:38:28,940 --> 00:38:32,280
I will not take as long to answer the second question as I did the first.

515
00:38:32,280 --> 00:38:34,780
Excuse me.

516
00:38:34,780 --> 00:38:42,360
When the earliest followers of Christ began to go out and proclaim the gospel of Jesus to the world around them,

517
00:38:42,820 --> 00:38:46,100
they are the ones that spent the most time with Jesus.

518
00:38:46,100 --> 00:38:47,320
They were trained by Jesus.

519
00:38:47,320 --> 00:38:51,200
They were commissioned by Jesus to go and preach the good news.

520
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:55,360
When the earliest Christ followers began to go out and proclaim the gospel,

521
00:38:55,360 --> 00:38:58,220
they gave an invitation for people to do three things.

522
00:38:58,220 --> 00:39:01,520
The first is to repent.

523
00:39:01,520 --> 00:39:03,760
The second is to believe.

524
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:06,140
And the third is to be baptized.

525
00:39:06,140 --> 00:39:08,420
Let's unpack those just really quickly.

526
00:39:08,420 --> 00:39:10,320
First, repent.

527
00:39:10,320 --> 00:39:15,000
Repentance is a changing of your mind.

528
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:19,280
When the earliest followers of Jesus would present the gospel, they would say,

529
00:39:19,460 --> 00:39:21,220
The kingdom of God is come.

530
00:39:21,220 --> 00:39:26,980
The time where God rules and reigns over all of his creation has come.

531
00:39:26,980 --> 00:39:31,960
And if you are living under the power of any other king,

532
00:39:31,960 --> 00:39:36,260
if you're living under the message of any other gospel,

533
00:39:36,260 --> 00:39:42,700
it's time to change your mind and submit your life to the kingdom of God on earth as it is in heaven.

534
00:39:44,460 --> 00:39:47,800
All of us, whether we like to believe it or know it or not,

535
00:39:47,800 --> 00:39:50,400
we all live our lives based on a gospel message.

536
00:39:50,400 --> 00:39:56,220
We all live our lives thinking salvation, thinking blessing will come through something.

537
00:39:56,220 --> 00:39:59,080
Whatever that something might be,

538
00:39:59,080 --> 00:40:02,180
whether you even have said it out loud or not,

539
00:40:02,180 --> 00:40:10,160
you might be living that your ability to provide for yourself through your job will bring you salvation.

540
00:40:10,160 --> 00:40:11,700
You'll get all the money you need.

541
00:40:11,700 --> 00:40:13,160
You'll retire early.

542
00:40:13,740 --> 00:40:16,900
Salvation will come to you through money, provision.

543
00:40:16,900 --> 00:40:18,360
That's a gospel.

544
00:40:18,360 --> 00:40:24,380
That is believing, putting your hope in something other than the God who created you.

545
00:40:24,380 --> 00:40:29,280
We all have a gospel, whether we say it out loud or not.

546
00:40:29,280 --> 00:40:31,560
And the early followers of Jesus said,

547
00:40:31,560 --> 00:40:36,680
If you're believing any other gospel than the gospel that Jesus is God

548
00:40:36,680 --> 00:40:39,460
and he came to establish God's kingdom on earth as it is in heaven,

549
00:40:39,460 --> 00:40:43,460
then you need to change your mind and you need to go in the direction of God's kingdom.

550
00:40:43,460 --> 00:40:46,000
So repent, change your mind.

551
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:47,680
Second, believe.

552
00:40:47,680 --> 00:40:50,920
I would say that believe is changing your allegiance.

553
00:40:50,920 --> 00:40:58,960
The word believe has often become in our gospel presentations as just an intellectual agreement.

554
00:40:59,080 --> 00:41:02,140
Yeah, I agree that Jesus was God and that he died for my sins.

555
00:41:02,140 --> 00:41:05,600
But in the Scriptures, belief is an active obedience.

556
00:41:05,600 --> 00:41:09,520
It is a walking in the direction of following behind Jesus.

557
00:41:10,520 --> 00:41:14,920
So the gospel writers, the gospel proclaimers, the early church said,

558
00:41:14,920 --> 00:41:20,480
repent of believing any other gospel and walk in step with Jesus.

559
00:41:20,480 --> 00:41:24,480
Follow his teachings to love your neighbor, to love your enemy as yourself.

560
00:41:25,800 --> 00:41:31,620
Submit to his teachings and you will receive salvation both now and for eternity.

561
00:41:31,620 --> 00:41:41,160
Lastly, they were invited to be baptized, to change your primary community.

562
00:41:41,340 --> 00:41:44,260
This is where it goes from individual to corporate.

563
00:41:44,260 --> 00:41:52,320
This is where it goes from a decision that I'm making on my own to I am actively telling a community of people that I have made this decision.

564
00:41:53,560 --> 00:41:54,420
And here's the deal.

565
00:41:54,420 --> 00:42:11,460
The church throughout most of its history has had differing opinions on baptism, including when and how it should be done.

566
00:42:11,460 --> 00:42:13,700
I don't have time to get into that this morning.

567
00:42:13,700 --> 00:42:19,620
I would just say that based on my reading of Scripture, a certain type of baptism isn't necessary for salvation,

568
00:42:19,620 --> 00:42:25,360
but it should be a very important, the very first, extremely important step in the process of salvation,

569
00:42:25,360 --> 00:42:28,860
because it tells the community around you that you have made this decision.

570
00:42:28,860 --> 00:42:32,900
And the gospel has implications for the entire community.

571
00:42:32,900 --> 00:42:38,640
So if you're in here and you're like, yeah, I've repented, I've believed, but you haven't told anybody,

572
00:42:38,640 --> 00:42:44,840
you're missing a very crucial, a very important part of the gospel.

573
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:49,140
This was included in all of the early followers' invitations.

574
00:42:49,620 --> 00:42:53,040
So, Donovan's supposed to be here somewhere.

575
00:42:53,040 --> 00:42:54,320
He might have missed the cue.

576
00:42:54,320 --> 00:43:00,960
Hey, buddy.

577
00:43:00,960 --> 00:43:07,060
How, you might ask, how do I know if I'm saved?

578
00:43:07,060 --> 00:43:16,240
Have you heard the good news about the inauguration of Christ's kingdom through his life, his teachings, his death, and his resurrection?

579
00:43:16,760 --> 00:43:20,320
Have you heard the announcement that the promised time has come?

580
00:43:20,320 --> 00:43:22,260
Jesus is here.

581
00:43:22,260 --> 00:43:24,820
He offers salvation and victory.

582
00:43:24,820 --> 00:43:25,860
Have you heard that news?

583
00:43:25,860 --> 00:43:29,340
Have you repented?

584
00:43:29,340 --> 00:43:34,200
Have you changed your mind about whatever other good news you were believing?

585
00:43:36,160 --> 00:43:39,120
And have you said, Jesus' news is the best news.

586
00:43:39,120 --> 00:43:40,140
It is the ultimate news.

587
00:43:40,140 --> 00:43:42,120
It is the only news.

588
00:43:42,120 --> 00:43:44,080
Have you repented?

589
00:43:44,080 --> 00:43:44,800
Have you changed your mind?

590
00:43:44,800 --> 00:43:45,440
Have you believed?

591
00:43:45,440 --> 00:43:50,540
Have you accepted the death and resurrection of Jesus on your behalf?

592
00:43:52,540 --> 00:44:00,720
for the forgiveness of your sins, for the transformation of you from the inside out so that you can be a blessing to the world around you?

593
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:06,880
And have you demonstrated that decision to your community through baptism?

594
00:44:06,880 --> 00:44:20,560
This is the clearest way I know how to explain if you've received the gospel, if you're saved or not.

595
00:44:20,560 --> 00:44:22,860
If you've done those things, if you've made that decision.

596
00:44:25,040 --> 00:44:27,400
If you have, you should be confident in your salvation.

597
00:44:27,400 --> 00:44:28,460
You will not be perfect.

598
00:44:28,460 --> 00:44:32,100
You might even walk away for a season.

599
00:44:32,100 --> 00:44:34,400
You might find yourself in rebellion.

600
00:44:34,400 --> 00:44:36,920
Think about the story of the prodigal son.

601
00:44:36,920 --> 00:44:38,860
He was part of the family.

602
00:44:38,860 --> 00:44:40,380
He walked away for a long time.

603
00:44:40,380 --> 00:44:41,740
Maybe that's you.

604
00:44:41,740 --> 00:44:42,760
Maybe you've walked away.

605
00:44:42,760 --> 00:44:45,020
You've made the decision once and you've walked away.

606
00:44:46,300 --> 00:44:48,900
May God draw you back to yourself, to himself.

607
00:44:48,900 --> 00:44:51,040
You won't be perfect.

608
00:44:51,040 --> 00:44:56,000
But if God has began a good work in you, he will continue.

609
00:44:56,000 --> 00:44:58,560
And you should participate with him.

610
00:44:58,560 --> 00:45:02,240
If you haven't been baptized, you should do so.

611
00:45:02,240 --> 00:45:06,540
I think we're planning to fill the tank next week.

612
00:45:06,540 --> 00:45:12,120
So if this is something that you haven't done and you feel the Lord leading you to do, please, let's have a conversation.

613
00:45:15,700 --> 00:45:24,140
I am going to do something that I do not do very often at all because I have had bad experiences as a child.

614
00:45:24,140 --> 00:45:27,540
And we all know what bad childhood experiences do to us as adults.

615
00:45:27,540 --> 00:45:29,800
Nothing bad ever, right?

616
00:45:29,800 --> 00:45:33,740
Some of you in therapy are like, yeah, let's not talk about it.

617
00:45:33,740 --> 00:45:38,780
I have a couple volunteers from the prayer team.

618
00:45:38,780 --> 00:45:42,240
If you want to come up to the prayer tent, I'm going to be there as well.

619
00:45:42,240 --> 00:45:44,120
We're going to do an old-fashioned altar call.

620
00:45:45,100 --> 00:45:58,120
If you have never publicly made a declaration, if you've never stepped across that line and made that decision that Jesus is your Savior, he is your Lord, he is the leader of your life.

621
00:45:58,120 --> 00:46:05,740
If you've never repented of your sins and trusted in Jesus, I just want to create an environment for you to make that decision today.

622
00:46:06,260 --> 00:46:12,680
If you're in here, you've already made that decision, I'd invite you throughout this time, we're going to sing a worship song, Oh, Come to the Altar.

623
00:46:12,680 --> 00:46:15,240
You're invited to come to the altar.

624
00:46:16,620 --> 00:46:31,900
If you've already made that decision, I'd ask you to sing the song, and as you sing, be in prayer for people in this room that have not yet made that decision, that the Holy Spirit would give them the courage, the power, the intentionality to make the decision for the first time.

625
00:46:31,900 --> 00:46:33,980
So we'll be up here.

626
00:46:33,980 --> 00:46:39,000
We'd love to have a conversation with you about what that looks like.

627
00:46:40,760 --> 00:46:41,780
And that's all I have.
